# Opt-in application groups. Selected by name in the answer file:
#
#   EXTRAS=office,containers
#
# Nothing here is installed unless asked for. A '## Requires:' line states that
# a group needs something beyond Arch's default repositories, and the installer
# enables it only when that group is chosen.

## Group: office
libreoffice-fresh

## Group: media
obs-studio
kdenlive
gimp

## Group: containers
docker
docker-compose
lazydocker

## Group: browsers
chromium

## Group: ai-local
ollama

## Group: gaming
## Requires: multilib
steam
lutris

## Group: desktop-tools
# Useful, not essential. Disks, processes, disk usage, keys, colour picking,
# screen recording, clipboard history, automounting.
gnome-disk-utility
gnome-system-monitor
baobab
seahorse
hyprpicker
wf-recorder
cliphist
udiskie

## Group: theming-gui
# Graphical theme and wallpaper editing, for people who would rather browse
# thumbnails than run a command.
#
# azote wants to OWN wallpaper setting - it launches its own backend. Archwright
# manages the wallpaper through a systemd unit and a symlink, so the two will
# fight if both are driving. Selecting this group is choosing azote's way; see
# the note in the README.
azote
nwg-look

## Group: printing
# A daemon and a print dialog. Clearly opt-in: a machine that never prints has
# no business running cupsd.
cups
system-config-printer
